Director Independence

Nasdaq listing standards require that a majority of the board of directors of a listed company be independent. An “independent director” is defined generally as a person other than an officer or employee of the company or its subsidiaries or any other individual having a relationship which in the opinion of the company’s board of directors, would interfere with the director’s exercise of independent judgment in carrying out the responsibilities of a director. Our board of directors has determined that Yungkong Bann, Michael E. Fuentes, and Rajiv Matthew are “independent directors” as defined in the Nasdaq listing standards and applicable SEC rules.
